            <title>[LU-21200] sanity-quota test_73b: MDS deadlock in quota pool lookup (qti_pools_add vs qsd_reint_qpool), suite TIMEOUT</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21200</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;sanity-quota test_73b ("default OST Pool Quotas limit for new user") hangs and the sanity-quota test set ends with "Timeout occurred after N minutes, last suite running was sanity-quota". It is a deadlock in the quota pool code on the MDS, not a data path failure.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The suite_log stops right after "set default quota for qpool1", i.e. at the runas dd in test_73b. The MDS stack_trace log from the timed out subtest shows about 55 mdt_rdpg threads blocked in rwsem_down_read_slowpath from qti_pools_add, one mdt thread blocked in rwsem_down_read_slowpath (cfs_hash_lookup / cfs_hash_multi_bd_lock), and qsd_reint_qpool blocked in rwsem_down_write_slowpath (cfs_hash_find_or_add / cfs_hash_multi_bd_lock). Clients are evicted/lose connection to MDT0000 while the hang lasts.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Frequency: rainshadow test sanity-quota test_73b shows 121 branch failures in 30 days (lustre-master-next 65, lustre-master 56), all TIMEOUT, first seen 2026-11-02, in full-part-2 (about 13-15% of runs) and full-dne-part-2 (17-25%). Reviews ran 6604 suite runs with a single TIMEOUT, on change 64875 (&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-19783" title="many fids with &amp;quot;fid2path: No data available&amp;quot;" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-19783"&gt;LU-19783&lt;/a&gt; lfsck, unrelated: the patch does not touch quota or the default pool quota path).&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Example failures:&lt;br/&gt;
master full-part-2 (same stack): &lt;a href="https://testing.whamcloud.com/sub_tests/a3490105-320a-441d-b648-88701ce9807a" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/sub_tests/a3490105-320a-441d-b648-88701ce9807a&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
review-zfs on change 64875 ps39: &lt;a href="https://testing.whamcloud.com/sub_tests/51859b9d-cc9b-42fe-809b-cc42995966c9" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/sub_tests/51859b9d-cc9b-42fe-809b-cc42995966c9&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;No existing ticket matches (&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-16448" title="sanity-quota test_3b: crashes in qsd_reint_qpool" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-16448"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-16448&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-17974" title="sanity-quota test_3b: (qmt_lock.c:957:qmt_id_lock_notify()) ASSERTION( lqe-&amp;gt;lqe_is_global )" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-17974"&gt;&lt;del&gt;LU-17974&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; are qsd_reint_qpool crashes, resolved). Likely a lock ordering problem between qsd_reint_qpool and qti_pools_add/lqe pool lookups (see the nested lqe lookup fix for test_73b).&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Raised by Patch Watcher run pw-engineer-64875-ps39-517a61d8daf3 on &lt;a href="https://review.whamcloud.com/64875" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/64875&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
